  </figure>
  <p>
    To finish this section, let me summarize with three points.
    First, there is mathematical way to create a linear regression by
    the least squares method: finding the best line by minimizing the
    residuals. Second, the numbers in that line carry statistical
    meaning: they encode the relationship between the data, at least
    approximately. Finally, those relationships can be extended to
    more variables. Extending to other numeric variables is just
    adding new terms to the equation, but to use categorical variables
    we have to assignment numbers to them, making them indicator
    variables. In all this, the coefficients carry the meaning of the
    relationship. 
  </p>
</section>

